---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const page = {
  title: "Write an ISO to a USB drive and verify it — Bootable",
  description: "Write an ISO to a removable USB drive. Review the drive, write the image, and verify the written bytes.",
  ogTitle: "Write an ISO to USB and verify it",
  ogDescription: "Choose an ISO and USB drive, then write and verify it.",
  ogType: "article",
  current: "guide",
  doc: { label: "Validation", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/docs/validation.md" },
  crumbs: [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides.html" }, { label: "Write ISO to USB" }],
};
---
<Layout {...page}>
<main class="guide-main">
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={page.crumbs} />
      <article>
        <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">ISO · USB</p><h1>Write an ISO to USB</h1><p class="lede">Choose an ISO and removable drive. Write the image and verify the written bytes.</p></header>
        <div class="guide-body">
          <div class="guide-content">
            <h2 id="inspection">Choose an ISO</h2>
            <p>Open a local ISO or choose one from the catalog. Linux and Unix hybrid ISOs use a raw write. Windows installer ISOs use the FAT32 media process.</p>
            <p>Bootable verifies a publisher checksum when available. A mismatch blocks writing.</p>

            <h2 id="target">Select the physical drive</h2>
            <p>Identify the drive by model, capacity, path, and serial suffix. Fixed, read-only, and system drives are not listed.</p>
            <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>The selected drive will be erased.</strong> Confirm the physical drive before writing.</p></div>

            <h2 id="steps">Write the ISO</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>Choose the ISO and wait for inspection to finish.</li>
              <li>Select the removable USB drive.</li>
              <li>Review the write method, operations, and drive identity.</li>
              <li>Confirm erasure.</li>
              <li>Start the write and keep the drive connected through verification.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>The write helper checks the drive identity and capacity again before writing.</p>

            <h2 id="readback">Verify the write</h2>
            <p>Bootable hashes the image while writing. It reads back the written range and compares SHA-256. Unused space is not checked.</p>
            <p>A match does not guarantee that the image will boot on every computer.</p>

            <h2 id="cancel">Cancellation</h2>
            <p>A cancelled write is marked incomplete. Rewrite the full image before using the drive.</p>

            <section class="related-guides"><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href="/compressed-image-writer">Write compressed images</a></li><li><a href="/verify-bootable-usb">Verification details</a></li><li><a href="/safe-usb-writer">Drive safety</a></li></ul></section>
            <div class="guide-cta"><h2>Install Bootable</h2><p>Use the desktop app or TUI.</p><a class="button primary" href="/download">View install steps</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-aside"><strong>On this page</strong><ul><li><a href="#inspection">Choose an ISO</a></li><li><a href="#target">Choose a drive</a></li><li><a href="#steps">Write the ISO</a></li><li><a href="#readback">Verify the write</a></li><li><a href="#cancel">Cancellation</a></li></ul></aside>
        </div>
      </article>
</main>
</Layout>
